\newlabel{alg:ladder}{{2}{13}{\textsc {WarmLadder}($K$, $k$, $c_{\max }$; $S$, $\beta $, $\gamma $, $p_{\mathrm {track}}$; per-rung budget $T_{\mathrm {rung}}$, guided weight factor $g\ge 1$, cap $g_{\max }$, max rungs $R_{\max }$). Extension of Algorithm~\ref {alg:anneal} by warm restart and guided reweighting}{algorithm.2}{}}
\citation{OLGB21}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Complete warm-start rung-ladder campaign on the dodecahedron boundary ($7776$ product facets of $K\times K$, $k=3$). Upper block: five long warm escalations ($c_{\max }=40$, $g=3$, $g_{\max }=11$), each reseeded from the previous incumbent. Lower block: $2.5$-minute ladder run unattended over $12$\,GPU-hours, summarised in batches of $20$ rungs; the final row combines the last partial batch with extended window probes and a $70$-trial basin survey. Mean gain per rung falls from $11.7$ in the first batch to below $1$ in the last; no complete cover was found. The obstacle is the sparsity of $K$: a dual-graph diameter of $7$ requires coordinated walks that grow geometrically harder to satisfy simultaneously as coverage rises.}}{14}{table.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:dodeca}{{4}{14}{Complete warm-start rung-ladder campaign on the dodecahedron boundary ($7776$ product facets of $K\times K$, $k=3$). Upper block: five long warm escalations ($c_{\max }=40$, $g=3$, $g_{\max }=11$), each reseeded from the previous incumbent. Lower block: $2.5$-minute ladder run unattended over $12$\,GPU-hours, summarised in batches of $20$ rungs; the final row combines the last partial batch with extended window probes and a $70$-trial basin survey. Mean gain per rung falls from $11.7$ in the first batch to below $1$ in the last; no complete cover was found. The obstacle is the sparsity of $K$: a dual-graph diameter of $7$ requires coordinated walks that grow geometrically harder to satisfy simultaneously as coverage rises}{table.caption.4}{}}
